WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.270
A story I never wanted to tell

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.006
our colleague and friend.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:06.806
Drew Griffin

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.842
passed away over the weekend.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.577
Drew, as you know,

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.645
was an outstanding journalist.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.114
What you may not have known

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.116
is that he was an even better human being

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.918
and in this business.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.521
TV journalism That is a rare quality.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.223
And though he would hate to hear

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.391
anyone say it,

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.126
preferring that his work

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.660
say everything that needs to be

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.395
said,

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:29.429
Drew Griffin,

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:32.065
truly was one of the good guys, the best.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:34.267
In fact, not just at CNN, but in life.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.969
He was he was tireless.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.303
He was honest.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.571
He was self-effacing.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.740
He was utterly devoted to his family.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.143
Every producer who ever worked with him

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.677
will tell you that on the road,

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:45.812
Drew was always thinking

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.113
about the fastest

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.382
and best way to do the story.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.684
So he could return home to them.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:52.952
You do the work.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.387
You do it better than anyone.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.356
But he couldn't wait to get home.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.625
And often his work changed.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.393
Government is investigations

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.094
into charity.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:01.861
Fraud

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.263
resulted in a nearly

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.931
$25 million settlement

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.099
with one of the largest direct

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.535
mail operators in the United States.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.570
His investigations into the way

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.605
the Veterans Administration was run

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.808
sparked a complete overhaul

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.076
of VA leadership

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.510
to change the way veterans

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.113
receive the care they need and deserve.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.349
Drew and his team earned a Peabody

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.451
Award for that work,

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.553
and he actually went to the ceremony.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.054
One of the rare exceptions

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.056
he made to the life he preferred,

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.124
which was away

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.726
from the spotlight allergic to accolades,

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.695
but drawn to the work,

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.230
drawn to the cause

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.298
and the ones his work

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.899
truly counted so much for.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.101
It showed in his talent

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.303
for getting people to talk to him,

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.438
which was frankly legendary, matched

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.106
only by his knack

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.274
for getting answers for those

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.742
who did not want

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.212
to give those answers to anyone.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.913
Unless you've tried to interview

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.014
someone who doesn't want to talk to you,

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.950
you can't truly appreciate

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.551
how difficult it is

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.421
And Drew was a master, fearless,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.056
even when the person in question

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.524
was a senator caught

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:05.692
in the act of doing the very thing

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.660
he had just spoken out against

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.597
getting cozy with high dollar lobbyists

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:11.931
after publicly chastising

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:12.966
that same kind of

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.567
business that, as usual,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:17.804
Just want to ask you why

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:18.872
they're so important.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:19.739
I mean, you're not the only guy

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:20.840
that does this.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.374
But I

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.742
didn't really consent to an interview

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.109
right now.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:23.610
And I

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.311
just wanted to ask you a few questions

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.480
about why you have these

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:27.947
in general,

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.816
why you have these kind of weekends

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.285
for these lobbyists who

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.586
politicians raise funds.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.455
And this is what we do.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:36.256
The way to do it.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:36.656
You spoke

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:39.559
so eloquently about the disconnected

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:40.560
not being representative.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.695
I just want it to like this.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:43.930
I enjoy scale.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.598
Thank you very much. Yeah.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:45.798
Thanks.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.332
A lot

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.538
As good as Drew was with the chase,

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:55.742
he was just as good at confronting lies

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.777
with facts.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.013
Why do you continue

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:00.980
to push the lie

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.149
that the 2020 election was stolen?

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.884
A lie? It's a lie. You have no proof.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.786
So we've looked at all the facts.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:07.620
You don't have the facts.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:09.956
Drew was

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.025
levelheaded, surefooted,

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.427
a truly genuine human being.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.128
And in a business

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.096
where cynicism is paramount.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.832
His sincerity shown through

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.967
his wife Margaret,

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.536
his three children, Ella Lui and Myles,

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.738
his two grandchildren.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.074
You're all in our thoughts tonight.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:31.544
Drew Griffin was just 60 years old.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.213
Laura,

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.082
so important to really address

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.483
and think about his legacy.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.851
And I just remember,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.419
you know, I'm

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.221
I'm pretty new to this business.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.223
And he would take the time

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.057
to write me

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.159
the nicest emails of encouragement

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.927
and just to say

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.063
words of wisdom, words of advice,

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.731
or just job well done

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.266
and to share and exchange

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:53.733
and the work

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.334
that he had done

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.501
as an informal mentor

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.636
in those ways

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:57.570
I'll never forget it

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.538
and I'll never forget the work

00:03:58.538 --> 00:03:59.305
that he has done.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.174
So I'm so glad to honor him tonight,

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.042
and I think I'll leave his family.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:04.510
You know,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.178
one of the things

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.213
I think about with him is

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.516
he had no partizan allegiances

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:11.751
whatsoever.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.486
He didn't care

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.622
if you were corrupt or you were lying

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.090
you're full of crap.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.091
He was coming after you.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.293
It did not matter

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.661
what party you belonged to

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.296
or even if you belong to a party.

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.497
He didn't care.

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.365
The news continues

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.399
CNN Tonight with John

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.101
Berman is next right after a quick break.

